"""FlyX lab: fly the DroneHacks course with machmoon/dronehacks-sim's waypoint controller.
Run:  python3 flyx_course/fly_course.py            (--shadow: everything except publishing to PX4)

GENERATED by flyx_course/build_fly_course.py from flyx_course/fly_course_template.py and
machmoon/dronehacks-sim@663cae6 (mission/core.py embedded verbatim, route mission/course.json).
Edit the template and rebuild; do not edit this file by hand. Self-contained: rclpy, px4_msgs,
std_msgs only.

THE ALGORITHM (friend's): a 15-waypoint route through the published course - first corridor, the
maze, Gate A, tunnel, chicane, window, landing approach - with per-segment speeds, an
acceleration limit, braking into each waypoint (sqrt(2 a d)), arrival within 8 cm before
advancing, and yaw toward the next waypoint. That logic is their CourseController, unchanged.

HOW IT FLIES PX4 HERE: the controller drives a virtual reference along the route (it is fed the
reference's own position/velocity, so it plans cleanly), and PX4 tracks a position target a short
lead ahead of it - never past the next waypoint - with partial velocity feedforward. A leash freezes the setpoint when the
real vehicle lags more than LEASH_M, so the commanded point never runs away from the drone and
stays on the route (>= 0.40 m from every wall for Sky Beta's 0.28 m radius on the published map).
Why not their raw velocity commands: in the FlyX lab this program can freeze for up to ~1.8 s
(measured, square runs), and PX4 keeps flying the last command meanwhile; a velocity command would
carry the drone on, a position on the route makes it stop there.

LAB ROBUSTNESS (from flyx_square, which completed in FlyX): fresh telemetry + 10 s settle before
arming; Offboard then arm; in the air odometry is the only liveness signal (pause > 0.4 s holds and
freezes the route, > 3 s lands), slow topics are latest-known state (fresh "estimator invalid"
lands, silence only after 10 s); PX4 leaving Offboard stops commanding; native Land at the end or
on any fault; Ctrl-C / lab Stop lands. Journal: flyx_course/runs/course-<time>/journal.jsonl
(else ~/flyx-runs, /tmp/flyx-runs).

Start ON THE LAUNCH MARK facing up the first corridor (course +y), after Reset world.
"""
SPEED_SCALE = 0.65   # friend's validated default for this route (Gazebo: 61.8 s, 0 contacts)
LEAD_S = 0.6        # PX4 position target leads the route reference by this (clamped at the next waypoint)
FF_FRAC = 0.4       # fraction of the reference velocity sent as feedforward
LEASH_M = 0.25       # freeze the route setpoint when the drone lags it by more than this
YAW_RATE_MAX = 0.25  # rad/s cap on the controller's yaw rate (theirs: 0.7). Visual odometry dies on
                     # fast turns: FlyX run 1 of this script lost xy ~3 s after the first maze corner at
                     # 0.5 rad/s; our failure maps had 30/40 deaths at yaw rates > 0.35 rad/s.
CORNER_DEG = 45.0    # waypoints turning more than this are "sharp corners"
CORNER_ZONE_M = 0.5  # approaching a sharp corner: brake at CORNER_ACC, no lead, no feedforward ...
CORNER_ACC = 0.3
CORNER_MIN_SPEED = 0.2   # ... but never below this: the turn happens while moving. A full stop
                         # turns the heading in place, which lost visual odometry in Gazebo v131.
DIVERGE_M = 0.8      # drone this far from the reference: the estimate or the vehicle is wrong, land
                     # (normal tracking <= 0.27 m in Gazebo; a 1.8 s program stall reaches ~0.63 m)
LAND_TOL_M = 0.15    # landing handoff reached when the drone is this close (course frame)
MAX_FLIGHT_S = 175.0 # rule 7.9: 3-minute run, margin
LAUNCH_XY = (-2.515, 0.914)   # launch mark, course frame (published map)
LAUNCH_HEADING = 1.5707963267948966   # facing up the first corridor (course +y)
ODOM_HOLD_S = 0.4    # odometry this old: hold (freeze the route) until it returns
OUTAGE_S = 3.0       # odometry missing this long in the air: land
SLOW_LOST_S = 10.0   # status / local position silent this long in the air: land
SETTLE_S = 10.0      # healthy + landed this long before Offboard/arm

